{"id":"n-20261014-5u749e","category":"sports","display_title":"Maccabi Questions EuroLeague Officiating","display_title_he":"מכבי מטילה ספק בשיפוט ביורוליג","short_summary":"Maccabi Tel Aviv is seeking explanations from the EuroLeague following a narrow 90-87 defeat to Barcelona, citing controversial refereeing decisions and a back injury to star guard Yam Madar.","english_level":"C1","words":476,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Maccabi_T.A_Cups.jpg/960px-Maccabi_T.A_Cups.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Reuven Frizi · CC BY-SA 3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maccabi_T.A_Cups.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Walla","domain":"sports.walla.co.il","url":"https://sports.walla.co.il/item/3872103","title":"מכבי תל אביב תדרוש תשובות על החלטות השיפוט: \"מרגיש לא טוב ולא נכון\"","published_at":"2026-10-14T07:20:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-14T07:20:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-14T06:17:21.581Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Maccabi Tel Aviv experienced profound frustration following a dramatic 90-87 defeat against Barcelona during the fifth round of the EuroLeague. This narrow loss dropped the yellow-and-blue squad to a disappointing 1-4 record in the competition. Members of the organization expressed strong dissatisfaction with the officiating, noting that several poor refereeing decisions ultimately prevented them from securing a victory. Team officials indicated they intend to demand formal clarifications from the EuroLeague regarding specific whistles during the match, most notably an unpenalized kicking violation by Barcelona player Tyrique Martin that struck Yam Madar, even after the referees reviewed the incident on the monitor. One team insider remarked that it feels entirely wrong and bad to leave the arena with such a terrible sensation, stressing that while they are careful not to speak publicly about referees, the missed calls changed the outcome. The match remained fiercely contested throughout, but Justin Robinson dashed Maccabi's hopes by hitting a decisive three-pointer with just 1.9 seconds remaining on the clock. Team representatives admitted that the defeat stings deeply, describing it as a missed opportunity to turn around their difficult start to the season, though they acknowledged they are improving on both ends of the floor.","Despite the unfavorable outcome, Yam Madar delivered a stellar performance that justified the club's major offseason investment in him. Stepping up impressively from the start of the second half, Madar kept his team in contention by scoring a career-high 22 points and earning a PIR index rating of 31. The club noted that they always knew he possessed this talent and hope he will replicate such displays in major victories soon. However, his stellar night ended on a painful note when he landed hard on his back during the controversial play that sparked Maccabi's anger toward the referees. Experiencing significant discomfort and having scored 39 points across his last two games—just 11 fewer than his entire previous season with Hapoel Tel Aviv—Madar will undergo treatments ahead of the upcoming match against Valencia in the hope of recovering sufficiently to display his usual form.","Teammate Bonzie Colson, who missed the final shot that could have forced overtime, reflected on the intense battle by noting that the squad can take many positive takeaways from the performance despite the painful result, calling it their first big test. Oshae Brissett echoed this sentiment, emphasizing that the team has demonstrated meaningful progress over the past week and a half and must continue pushing forward in the highly competitive EuroLeague environment where top-tier opponents await every night, requiring them to study the video and keep fighting hard.","Following their stay in Barcelona, the Maccabi delegation planned a road journey to Valencia after completing a light concluding training session designed to avoid overtaxing the players. The schedule also includes an initial video briefing regarding Valencia, who suffered a dramatic loss to Panathinaikos and currently exhibit exceptional form."],"facts":[{"fact":"Maccabi Tel Aviv lost 90-87 to Barcelona in the fifth round of the EuroLeague, dropping to a 1-4 record.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Maccabi plans to demand answers from the EuroLeague regarding specific refereeing decisions, including an ignored kicking violation against Tyrique Martin involving Yam Madar, despite a monitor review.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Yam Madar scored a career-high 22 points with an index rating of 31, but suffered a back injury during the controversial play and requires treatment ahead of the Valencia game.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Justin Robinson scored a crucial three-pointer for Barcelona with 1.9 seconds remaining to seal the game.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Bonzie Colson missed the final shot to force overtime, while Oshae Brissett noted the team's progress.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Maccabi will travel by road from Barcelona to Valencia for their upcoming match after holding a light training session.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Maccabi Tel Aviv","lemma":"Maccabi Tel Aviv","pos":"proper noun","he":"מכבי תל אביב","name":"Maccabi Tel Aviv"},{"text":"experienced","lemma":"experience","pos":"verb","he":"חווה","name":""},{"text":"profound","lemma":"profound","pos":"adjective","he":"עמוק","name":""},{"text":"frustration","lemma":"frustration","pos":"noun","he":"תסכול","name":""},{"text":"following","lemma":"follow","pos":"preposition","he":"בעקבות","name":""},{"text":"dramatic","lemma":"dramatic","pos":"adjective","he":"דרמטי","name":""},{"text":"defeat","lemma":"defeat","pos":"noun","he":"הפסד","name":""},{"text":"against","lemma":"against","pos":"preposition","he":"נגד","name":""},{"text":"